# Protection flags for benchmark/corpus_typeconf/ -- TYPE CONFUSION THROUGH AN
# ATTACKER-CONTROLLED UNION TAG (CWE-843).
#
# HELD IDENTICAL ACROSS EVERY TARGET IN THIS FAMILY ON PURPOSE. The only thing
# that varies between targets is HOW THE TAG COMES TO DISAGREE WITH THE DATA
# (inside set_tag() or reset_cell()); everything else -- the menu, the record
# layout, the union's three arms, the leak channel, the tag-guarded indirect
# call, win() -- is the same program. A protection difference between two
# targets would confound that measurement, so a target that lost this file and
# was rebuilt at gcc's defaults would be measuring a different challenge.
#
# -fstack-protector-all  canary=ON. The hijack lands on a `call *<reg>` in the
#                        MIDDLE of invoke_cell(), not on a saved return address,
#                        so the epilogue check is never reached and the canary
#                        is structurally irrelevant here. It is ON anyway, so
#                        that "hardened" cannot be quietly re-learned as "not
#                        exploitable" -- and so that a failure can never be
#                        blamed on a protection this category does not touch.
# -pie -fPIE             PIE=ON. Makes a code-address leak MANDATORY: win()'s
#                        address is unknown until show() has dumped a freshly
#                        created cell and disclosed the default_cell pointer the
#                        program itself installed in the union's pointer arm.
#                        This is what forces the exploit to use the program's
#                        own honest use of the pointer arm before abusing it.
# -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now    RELRO=FULL. The GOT is read-only, so "write win() over
#                        a GOT slot" is STRUCTURALLY unavailable and the only
#                        writable code pointer in the process is the one this
#                        category is about: the union's pointer arm inside a
#                        heap-allocated cell.
# -O0                    REQUIRED, and the one flag here that is not a choice.
#                        Two things must survive the compiler or the target
#                        silently stops being in this category at all:
#                          * the UNION must stay a union at one address -- at
#                            higher -O gcc is free to keep `u.num` in a register
#                            across the store/reload, or to collapse arms it can
#                            prove are never both live, and then the integer the
#                            operator wrote is no longer the bytes the pointer
#                            read sees;
#                          * `c->u.fn()` must stay an INDIRECT call reloaded from
#                            the record. gcc can devirtualise it to a direct
#                            `call default_cell` when it can see the only store,
#                            which removes the destination this family aims at.
#                        Also keeps `int tag` a real memory field at +0 instead
#                        of a value tracked in a register, which is what the
#                        mis-tag is measured on.
#
# NX is ON (default, no -z execstack).
#
# BUILT AND TESTED AGAINST -- MEASURED ON THIS HOST 2026-09-28, not copied
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   glibc   2.35   (Ubuntu GLIBC 2.35-0ubuntu3.15)   <-- `ldd --version`
#   gcc     11.4.0 (Ubuntu 11.4.0-1ubuntu1~22.04.3)  <-- `gcc --version`
#   kernel  6.8.0-138-generic x86-64, Ubuntu 22.04   <-- `uname -r`
#
# Version-sensitive facts this family depends on:
#   * `realloc(p, sizeof *p)` on a live chunk of exactly that size returns the
#     SAME pointer on glibc (no copy, no move), which is what makes tc_13's
#     stale tag land on the same record it was saved from. A reader on another
#     allocator MUST re-check this before comparing results.
#   * nothing else. There is no chunk-layout arithmetic, no freelist, and no
#     allocator metadata anywhere in this family -- deliberately, because those
#     are benchmark/corpus_heap_variants/'s and corpus_allocsize/'s primitives
#     and their absence is what makes a solve here attributable to the tag.
-fstack-protector-all
-pie
-fPIE
-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now
-O0
